# Local working files: editor and assistant config, internal notes, old release
# assets. Some of these are tracked in the maintainer's own checkout, which is
# not a contradiction, since gitignore does not untrack an already-tracked file.
# The entries are a safety net, so do not remove them as redundant: they are
# what stops these paths being staged by accident in a clone that should not
# carry them.
.claude/
.vscode/
docs/QA.md
docs/PUBLISHING.md
public/release-notes/
.publicignore
